"answer": "Project Zenith is a Q3 2023 initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions for enhanced security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project involves gathering innovative ideas, particularly from R&D, to leverage AI for data visualization and efficiency improvements. Key developments include the expansion of the team with experts in machine learning and cloud computing, and the exploration of a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology. Financially, the training budget has been approved at $15,000, and the compliance plan budget has been increased to $55,000. Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective January next year. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% increase in efficiency, with further discussions scheduled for August 5th. Stakeholder feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November."
